---
title: RNG - true random number generator, nothing to wire
---
%% ON-CHIP ONLY. No pins.
%% Entropy comes from an analog noise source, not a software PRNG.
%% Needs its own 48 MHz-capable clock domain enabled before it will produce
%% anything; check the seed and clock error flags on every read.
flowchart LR
    subgraph MCU["STM32F429I-DISC1"]
        NOISE["Analog noise source - ring oscillators"]
        LFSR["Conditioning / LFSR"]
        DR["RNG_DR - 32-bit output"]
        SR["RNG_SR - DRDY, SEIS seed error, CEIS clock error"]
        APP["Application"]
    end

    NOISE --> LFSR
    LFSR --> DR
    LFSR --> SR
    SR -->|"check before trusting DR"| APP
    DR --> APP
